    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="0543" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1948v03/pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860S.00/4–1648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-04-16T13:00:00+01:00">April 16, 1948—1
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Niact 2000. Foreign Office and British Embassy
                    both inform me that agreement has been reached between US, UK and France
                    regarding reply to Soviet note of April 13<anchor n="1" xml:id="d330-f1"/> re
                    Trieste (my 1981 April 15).<anchor n="2" xml:id="d330-f2"/> The French will make
                    public their reply tonight at midnight which is 6 p. m. EST.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d330-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department 2000, repeated London 298, Rome 182.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d330-f1" n="1" xml:id="d330-f1-content"> For the English translation of
                the text of the Soviet note of April 13, see the Department of State <hi
                    rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, April 26, 1948, p. 549. <p>In telegram 1733
                    of April 14, note printed, Dunn reported that the Soviet rejection of the
                    proposal to return Trieste to Italy was prominently reported in most of the Rome
                    newspapers (860S.00/4–1448).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d330-f2" n="2" xml:id="d330-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed (860S.00/4–1648).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d330-f3" n="3" xml:id="d330-f3-content"> In despatch No. 571, April 19,
                not printed, Caffery forwarded the text of the French note delivered to the Soviet
                Ambassador on April 16 (860S.00/4–1948). <p>The text of the note delivered by the
                    Department to the Soviet Embassy in Washington, and released to the press at
                    2300 hours GMT April 16, was sent to London in Niact 1355 which was repeated to Paris, Rome, Moscow, Trieste and
                    Belgrade, not printed (860S.00/4–1648). For text see Department of State
                    bulletin, April 25, 1948, p. 549.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
